WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.620 --> 00:00:05.129
The biggest question leading into the release
of Marvel's superhero blockbuster Black Panther

00:00:05.129 --> 00:00:08.340
was: can it possibly live up to the massive
amount of hype?

00:00:08.340 --> 00:00:12.380
Well, that question has been answered with
a resounding yes, as millions of ecstatic

00:00:12.380 --> 00:00:13.660
fans around the world can attest.

00:00:13.860 --> 00:00:17.880
But as great as the film is, there are some
other questions it never quite got around

00:00:17.880 --> 00:00:18.440
to addressing.

00:00:18.580 --> 00:00:22.780
So grab your vibranium and hold on tight,
because here's a spoiler-filled look at some

00:00:22.780 --> 00:00:25.220
of the biggest unanswered questions in Black
Panther.

00:00:25.560 --> 00:00:27.520
Why didn't they bring the kid to Wakanda?

00:00:27.800 --> 00:00:33.000
After King T'Chaka kills his brother, he heads
home to Wakanda, leaving his suddenly orphaned

00:00:33.000 --> 00:00:34.620
nephew Erik behind in Oakland.

00:00:34.860 --> 00:00:38.720
This ends up being a terrible mistake, as
the embittered boy grows up to become the

00:00:38.720 --> 00:00:40.260
conquering invader Killmonger.

00:00:40.560 --> 00:00:45.160
Sure, hindsight is 20-20, but you have to
ask: why did T'Chaka leave the boy behind?

00:00:45.320 --> 00:00:49.670
In the film, it's said multiple times that
he did it to protect the veil of secrecy surrounding

00:00:49.670 --> 00:00:50.180
Wakanda.

00:00:50.340 --> 00:00:55.000
But how exactly would adopting an orphaned
little boy threaten national security?

00:00:55.120 --> 00:00:58.820
It doesn't seem like anybody in Oakland would
have missed him, and bringing the child — and

00:00:58.820 --> 00:01:02.460
his father's body — back to Wakanda would
have tied up loose ends instead of leaving

00:01:02.460 --> 00:01:02.960
them.

00:01:03.160 --> 00:01:04.820
Plus, it's just the right thing to do.

00:01:04.820 --> 00:01:08.960
Leaving the boy behind is a real head-scratcher
— not to mention a total jerk move.

00:01:09.120 --> 00:01:11.480
Is T'Challa the last Black Panther?

00:01:11.800 --> 00:01:16.740
In a pivotal scene, after Killmonger becomes
the new king of Wakanda, he orders the botanists

00:01:16.750 --> 00:01:21.150
in the garden of heart-shaped herbs to burn
the country's entire supply of the magic plant

00:01:21.150 --> 00:01:23.700
that gives their monarchs the power of the
Black Panther.

00:01:24.240 --> 00:01:28.000
So does that actually mean that T'Challa is
the last of the Black Panthers?

00:01:28.190 --> 00:01:32.440
The comics tell us that the super-plants exist
in the first place because vibranium mutates

00:01:32.450 --> 00:01:36.920
the local flora — so wouldn't the presence
of a massive mountain of vibranium mean it

00:01:36.920 --> 00:01:38.160
would just… create more?

00:01:38.360 --> 00:01:43.070
Plus, Nakia shows just how easy to simply
walk out the door with one in your pocket,

00:01:43.070 --> 00:01:44.760
so there could be a supply pretty much anywhere.

00:01:44.960 --> 00:01:45.940
But is there?

00:01:45.940 --> 00:01:48.120
Or is this the end of the Black Panther legacy?

00:01:48.380 --> 00:01:51.860
We just don't know enough about how the whole
Black Panther thing works to say.

00:01:51.860 --> 00:01:52.540
Speaking of which…

00:01:52.960 --> 00:01:55.230
How does the whole Black Panther thing work?

00:01:55.480 --> 00:02:00.060
So, according to the movie, the powers of
the Panther-goddess Bast are bestowed upon

00:02:00.060 --> 00:02:03.740
the reigning monarch of Wakanda after they
eat the magic heart-shaped herb.

00:02:03.780 --> 00:02:08.000
Then the monarch is buried alive while their
spirit travels to the afterlife to commune

00:02:08.000 --> 00:02:12.420
with the spirits of their ancestors, before
being reborn as…the Black Panther!

00:02:12.560 --> 00:02:17.080
One big question, though: in Captain America:
Civil War, it seems as though T'Challa has

00:02:17.090 --> 00:02:22.190
already become Black Panther before his father's
death, something verified by the official

00:02:22.190 --> 00:02:22.980
prequel comics.

00:02:23.220 --> 00:02:25.780
So who exactly can become Black Panther?

00:02:25.780 --> 00:02:30.069
The movie suggests only the king is allowed
to eat the heart-shaped herb, but that's clearly

00:02:30.069 --> 00:02:30.680
not true.

00:02:30.880 --> 00:02:35.280
It doesn't seem hereditary either, considering
the kingship is sometimes determined by ritual

00:02:35.280 --> 00:02:36.660
combat and not bloodlines.

00:02:36.920 --> 00:02:40.760
So can anyone become Black Panther if the
king appoints them to the role?

00:02:40.769 --> 00:02:45.530
And if so, doesn't it seem negligent for the
nation's supreme leader to be constantly courting

00:02:45.530 --> 00:02:49.680
death by battling supervillains, instead of
delegating that responsibility to someone

00:02:49.680 --> 00:02:50.500
more expendable?

00:02:50.640 --> 00:02:54.060
This is one area where we're more confused
than before the movie started.

00:02:54.180 --> 00:02:56.180
What does vibranium actually do?

00:02:56.760 --> 00:02:58.980
It's supposed to be the hardest metal in the
world.

00:02:59.100 --> 00:03:04.580
But vibranium also seems to have magic powers,
like mutating the plants in Wakanda, and enabling

00:03:04.580 --> 00:03:09.360
Wakandan technology to do all sorts of random
things that, well, maybe don't make much sense.

00:03:09.640 --> 00:03:15.040
For instance, how does jamming a wad of vibranium
into an open gunshot wound stabilize a spinal

00:03:15.040 --> 00:03:15.540
injury?

00:03:15.600 --> 00:03:20.220
It seems as though vibranium's main property
is covering over plot holes, which makes it

00:03:20.220 --> 00:03:21.900
a very valuable resource indeed.

00:03:22.020 --> 00:03:23.320
And then there's that suit...

00:03:23.520 --> 00:03:26.000
Does every Marvel hero need a super suit?

00:03:26.300 --> 00:03:29.920
Thanks to the heart-shaped herb, Black Panther
possesses inhuman speed, agility, strength,

00:03:29.920 --> 00:03:31.600
and stamina.

00:03:31.820 --> 00:03:36.200
Yet over the course of Black Panther, most
of the major butt-kicking moves he pulls off

00:03:36.200 --> 00:03:40.299
during the fight scenes are possible because
he's wearing a technologically advanced super

00:03:40.299 --> 00:03:44.830
suit that allows him to stop bullets and then
redirect the absorbed kinetic energy into

00:03:44.830 --> 00:03:45.940
concussive blasts.

00:03:46.200 --> 00:03:48.519
Which would be totally cool in Iron Man 4.

00:03:48.520 --> 00:03:51.240
But does every single Marvel hero need a super
suit?

00:03:51.240 --> 00:03:53.860
It's fine for Iron Man and War Machine.

00:03:53.900 --> 00:03:54.900
And Ant-Man.

00:03:55.260 --> 00:03:55.760
And the Wasp.

00:03:56.360 --> 00:03:57.080
And the Falcon.

00:03:57.220 --> 00:04:01.920
But when Marvel sticks characters like Spider-Man
and Black Panther into super suits, it all

00:04:01.920 --> 00:04:03.480
starts to feel very samey-samey.

00:04:03.700 --> 00:04:08.379
And ironically, the most compelling and gripping
fights in Black Panther are the ritual challenges

00:04:08.380 --> 00:04:10.940
where T'Challa is stripped of his powers and
gizmos.

00:04:11.120 --> 00:04:14.560
So why does Marvel insist on giving everyone
these super suits?

00:04:14.860 --> 00:04:17.480
T'Challa seems pretty super without it, y'know.

00:04:18.000 --> 00:04:19.840
How does Wakanda function?

00:04:20.060 --> 00:04:24.920
According to the movie, Wakanda has been isolated
for centuries, hiding itself away to make

00:04:24.920 --> 00:04:27.700
sure nobody else gets any of its precious
vibranium.

00:04:27.900 --> 00:04:31.800
But if they're unwilling to trade their most
valuable resource, where do they get… everything

00:04:31.800 --> 00:04:32.300
else?

00:04:32.680 --> 00:04:37.800
Sure, vibranium can do all sorts of amazing
things, but you can't build an entire technologically

00:04:37.800 --> 00:04:40.520
superior society out of one rock...can you?

00:04:40.680 --> 00:04:44.440
They seem to have a massive amount of wealth,
but where does it come from if they really

00:04:44.440 --> 00:04:46.330
are as isolated as they claim to be?

00:04:46.330 --> 00:04:50.840
And if they're so peaceful and insular, why
exactly do they have enclaves of highly trained

00:04:50.840 --> 00:04:54.640
spies and soldiers secretly stationed in all
the major centers of the world?

00:04:54.780 --> 00:04:58.780
And not just major centers — they have so
many "war dogs" around the world that they

00:04:58.780 --> 00:05:02.919
even have a base in Oakland, which isn't even
among the top one-thousand largest cities

00:05:02.920 --> 00:05:03.460
in the world.

00:05:03.660 --> 00:05:07.460
So why does Wakanda really have such an extensive
worldwide military operation?

00:05:08.760 --> 00:05:09.260
Now what?

00:05:09.940 --> 00:05:14.100
Maybe the biggest question left unanswered
from Black Panther is one they never intended

00:05:14.100 --> 00:05:15.020
to answer in this movie.

00:05:15.220 --> 00:05:16.500
Namely, what comes next?

00:05:16.680 --> 00:05:21.300
We know from the trailer to Avengers: Infinity
War that Thanos is going to attack Wakanda

00:05:21.300 --> 00:05:25.340
— presumably because an Infinity Stone is
there, or somehow ends up there.

00:05:25.389 --> 00:05:29.820
We also know from the trailer that Captain
America and a team of Avengers are on hand

00:05:29.820 --> 00:05:31.340
in Wakanda when this happens.

00:05:31.460 --> 00:05:33.300
So how does that all come about?

00:05:33.300 --> 00:05:35.860
And what's going to happen to T'Challa and
Wakanda?

00:05:35.860 --> 00:05:39.319
Is their big push to become an open nation
going to end before it even gets a chance

00:05:39.320 --> 00:05:39.820
to start?

00:05:40.040 --> 00:05:42.860
Or are they just going to be left sharing
a huge pile of rubble?

00:05:42.860 --> 00:05:46.720
It seems there's only one way to find out,
and all we can say is that we can't wait to

00:05:46.729 --> 00:05:51.110
see what unanswered questions are still left
after we watch Avengers: Infinity War — and

00:05:51.110 --> 00:05:52.060
Black Panther 2.

00:05:52.280 --> 00:05:53.020
Thanks for watching!

00:05:53.280 --> 00:05:55.400
